post.description:
Send one or more contact cards via WhatsApp.

Contact cards allow sharing contact information including names, phone numbers,
email addresses, physical addresses, and organization details.
Currently supported on **WhatsApp only**.

## Contact Card Structure

Each contact must have at minimum a `name.formatted_name`. Optionally include:
- **phones**: List of phone numbers with type (CELL, WORK, HOME, etc.)
- **emails**: List of email addresses with type
- **addresses**: Physical addresses
- **org**: Organization/company information
- **urls**: Website URLs
- **birthday**: Date of birth (YYYY-MM-DD)

## Example Request
```json
{
    "channel_id": "uuid",
    "contact_id": "uuid",
    "contacts": [
        {
            "name": {
                "formatted_name": "John Doe",
                "first_name": "John",
                "last_name": "Doe"
            },
            "phones": [
                {"phone": "+1234567890", "type": "CELL"}
            ],
            "emails": [
                {"email": "john@example.com", "type": "WORK"}
            ],
            "org": {
                "company": "Acme Inc",
                "title": "Software Engineer"
            }
        }
    ]
}
```

**Required Scopes:** `messages:create`

Search for similar conversations based on query text using Vertex AI RAG.

**Required Scopes:** `conversations:read`

Request body: {"query_text": "...", "limit": 5}

Create a new email template with variable system

**Required Scopes:** `email:create`

- Define structural framework with MJML
- Use {{variable_name}} placeholders for customization
- Set color palette and fonts for brand consistency
- MJML is validated and compiled to HTML on creation
- Variables use lowercase_with_underscores naming convention

**Variable System:**
- Template variables: {{hero_title}}, {{cta_url}}, {{main_content}}
- Contact variables: {{contact.name}}, {{contact.email}}
- Company variables: {{company.name}}
- System variables: {{system.year}}

Check if current user has required scopes

Useful for frontend to check multiple permissions at once

Example:
POST /api/v1/permissions/me/check
{
    "required_scopes": ["campaigns:update", "email:read", "lists:*"]
}

Returns:
{
    "has_all": true,
    "results": {
        "campaigns:update": true,
        "email:read": true,
        "lists:*": true
    }
}

